    "title": "Pepsi, Food City unveil 1981 Mountain Dew Buick Regal inspired by Darrell Waltrip - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Faith Little ,\n1 hours ago\nABINGDON, Va. (WJHL) — Pepsi and Food City unveiled a new “Mountain Dew” car on Wednesday, inspired by NASCAR legend Darrell Waltrip’s 1981 Buick Regal.\nThe car will travel to Food City locations and other events, offering opportunities for people to take pictures and enjoy free Mountain Dew samples.\nThe Buick was painted in honor of Waltrip’s 1981 appearance in the NASCAR championship. The car has a Mountain Dew “Number 48” paint job to honor the year the drink was created in Johnson City.\nFrontier Health highlights signs of domestic violence and resources for survivors “We’re going to sample products at our store, hand out coupons at the store, and we’ll have some great deals on Mountain Dew,” Food City’s V.P. of Merchandising Ross Purdy said. “In addition to that, one lucky customer will have the opportunity to win $25,000 that will be presented to them right before Christmas. And it’s a simple process. Anytime you buy a Mountain Dew and you use your value card, you’re automatically registered to win.”\nPepsico Beverages Key Account Manager Jason Smith said community members can keep an eye out for future events that will host the car.\n“Back in 1981, Darrell Waltrip won the NASCAR national championship with the 1981 Buick. And so we have replicated that 1981 Buick, with the number 48 for the year that Mountain Dew was born,” he said. “And, again, this vehicle will be used as a marketing idea, marketing plan for joint efforts between Mountain Dew and Food City for grand openings, community events, and things of that nature.”\nThe car also has a 400-hp Chevy engine and a trunk stocked full of Mountain Dew.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJHL | Tri-Cities News & Weather.",
